To determine if a given integer \( n \) is a power of three without using loops or recursion, we can leverage mathematical properties and precomputed values. Specifically, we can use the fact that the highest power of three within the 32-bit signed integer range is \( 3^{19} = 1162261467 \). Any higher power of three will exceed the maximum value of a 32-bit signed integer.

Here's a Java method to solve this problem:

```java
public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    // Check if n is positive and if it divides into 1162261467 exactly
    return n > 0 && (1162261467 % n == 0);
}
```

